cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use carbon-cost or its tariff data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "carbon-cost: road tolls and carbon charges per truck trip in Europe"
abstract: >-
  carbon-cost works out what a truck trip pays in road tolls and carbon
  charges, per country and per charge, with the CO2 part shown separately:
  km-based tolls split into their legal parts (infrastructure, air, noise,
  CO2), entry-to-exit and per-passage tolls, vignettes, bridge and tunnel
  tolls, EU ETS on ferry crossings, ETS2 on road fuel from 2028 and national
  CO2 prices on diesel. Every rate is taken from the law or the official
  tariff that sets it, fetched by script and stored in the Open Road Charge
  Tariff (ORCT) format. Routes and emissions come from Sootcase (GLEC
  Framework, ISO 14083).
authors:
  - family-names: Ghafouri
    given-names: Majid
repository-code: "https://github.com/majidkabir/carbon-cost"
url: "https://sootcase.org/carbon-cost/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - road tolls
  - road user charges
  - truck tolls
  - Eurovignette
  - CO2 emission class
  - carbon pricing
  - EU ETS
  - ETS2
  - freight transport
  - road freight emissions
  - ORCT
